        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: चकित",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चकित — cakit — \"taken aback; astonished\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मीरा का नया घर देखकर सब चकित थे। Mīrā kā nayā ghar dekhkar sab cakit the. Everyone was astonished when they saw Mira's new house."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चकित (cakit) is a tatsama, borrowed from Sanskrit cakita, \"trembling, timid, startled\" (Monier-Williams). Hindi has turned the start of fright into the start of surprise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
